  "problem": "$12\\times \\frac{1}{3}=$",
  "worked_solution": "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12\\times 1}{3}=\\frac{12}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n12÷3=4\n$$",
